    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This residence which was originally constructed circa 1929 is contemporary in layout and design and presents an opportunity to acquire an excellent standard of accommodation situated in a desirable and scenic location. There are many attractive features.\n\nENTRANCE HALL:2.45m x 1.45m + 1.00m x 2.40m\nCeramic tile over concrete floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling. Wall hung central heating radiator.\n\nHOT PRESS:0.55m x 1.45m\nTimber over concrete floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling.\n\nHALL TO BEDROOM 1 & \nBATHROOM:Suspended timber floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling.\n\nBEDROOM 1:3.35m x 2.35m\nSuspended timber floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling. Wall hung central heating radiator.\n\nBATHROOM:2.80m x 1.95m\nCeramic tile over concrete floor. Walls extensively tiled in ceramic & part painted. Ceramic tile to ceiling in bath surround. Painted ceiling. Wall hung towel radiator. Stand-in bath shower. Ceramic wash hand basin with timber surround, under-sink cabinets and timber over-sink vanity unit. Pan.\n\nKITCHEN / DINING ROOM:8.40m x 3.00m\nSuspended timber floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling. Wall hung central heating radiator. Galley-style kitchen. Storage units under & over worktop. Ceramic tile splashback. Plentiful storage. Ceramic hob, oven and dishwasher. Exit door to garden from dining area. \n\nSITTING ROOM:6.85m x 4.15m (- 2.45m x 1.60m)\nSuspended timber floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling. Wall hung central heating radiator. Solid fuel burning stove, enabled for central heating. Double patio doors to garden. Open plan to kitchen/dining room. \nHALLWAY \nTO BEDROOMS 2 & 3:3.40m x 0.85m\nSuspended timber floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling.\n\nBEDROOM 2:4.15m x 1.95m\nSuspended timber floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling. Wall hung central heating radiator. Extensive built-in wardrobe storage.\n\nMASTER BEDROOM:3.00m x 3.30m\nSuspended timber floor. Painted plastered walls and ceiling. Wall hung central heating radiator.\n\nENSUITE:2.25m x 1.45m\nCeramic tile over suspended timber floor. Wall hung central heating radiator Walls extensively tiled in ceramic and part painted. Shower cubicle housing electric shower. Wash hand basin and pedestal. Pan.\n\nThis property is in excellent decorative order. Outside at front is an area adequate for the parking of two cars. A steel workshop accessible by door from front and side is situated at the side of the residence.\n\nThe overall accommodation area measures approximately 95 square metres (1022 sq ft). The overall site area measures approximately 0.15 Hectares (1,500 square metres).\n\n\nSERVICES\n\nWater provided by a group water scheme, drainage to a septic tank, mains electricity, dual central heating."
      },
